From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: explorer: the shell's desktop icons

The desktop showed only shortcuts from the Desktop folders; Windows shows
its own icons too -- by default the Recycle Bin, and This PC, the user's
files, Network and Control Panel when Desktop Icon Settings turns them on
(HKCU\...\Explorer\HideDesktopIcons\NewStartPanel, {CLSID} = 0). Now the
desktop honours that, with Windows 10's names, their shell icons, and a
double-click opening the folder (or the Control Panel).

- Icons fill columns top to bottom, as on Windows, above the taskbar.
- Titles have a shadow, so they read on any wallpaper.
- explorer.exe ::{CLSID} opens that shell folder: the root is not a file
  path, so GetFullPathName turned it into "::\{...}" and no folder opened.

Gate: test/desktop-icons-gate.sh.
